WEBVTT

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:17.610
AUTUMN 1995

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.180
Thanks for getting the souvenir for Akira.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.320
Here, as thanks for today.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.790
TOKIMEKI MEMORIAL

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.390
A game?

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:29.590
You need to play that
and study what women want.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.530
What women want?

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:02.760
What? You're playing <i>Tokimeki Memorial?</i>

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:06.500
Yeah, I'm supposed to study
what women want.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.030
You? You know
absolutely zero about romance.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.570
You'll study what women want?

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.000
"Absolutely zero"?

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.770
<i>So you're doing it for Ono, right?</i>

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:16.970
<i>That pisses me off.</i>

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:18.870
-Give it back!
-Huh?

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.210
Give me back my PlayStation right now!

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:22.810
Hey young man!

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.950
I'm back again!

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.750
Hurry, let me see you play
<i>Tokimeki Memorial!</i>

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:29.820
Ono's big sis...

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:34.120
I actually have to give the PlayStation
back to Hidaka here.

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:35.920
W-What did you say?

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.390
<i>Ono's big sister?</i>

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:43.030
<i>It's true I usually like having </i>
<i>other people watch me play...</i>

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:44.900
<i>But my mom,</i>

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.040
<i>Ono's sis and...</i>

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.700
<i>Hidaka, too?</i>

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:49.840
Aren't you glad?

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:53.240
Hidaka says you can return
her PlayStation at a later date.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:56.980
I also want to watch Yaguchi play
<i>Tokimeki Memorial.</i>

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.780
Why do they want to
watch me play<i> this</i> game...

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:06.050
<i>They're just enjoying </i>
<i>watching a man struggle.</i>

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.200
<i>It's the portable version of the famous</i>
<i>dating simulation game.</i>

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:20.340
<i>You increase the love meter of </i>
<i>different girls at your school,</i>

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.810
<i>and your goal is a confession of love</i>
<i>under the legendary tree.</i>

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.810
Oh, another date at the arcade?

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:30.010
I'll say I like shooting.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:34.620
<i>I think this game is too hard for me...</i>

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.990
Oh, you didn't make a good impression!

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.890
You're supposed to say
you like crane games!

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.230
I'm choosing the options
I sincerely think are better.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:45.630
What's wrong with that?

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:49.930
<i>This is where we came before.</i>
<i>I'm a little tired of it...</i>

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:51.830
See? She called you out.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:54.600
You can't just do things you think is fun.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:57.840
Put yourself in a woman's shoes
to guess what she wants.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.110
-I don't get it...
<i>-If it were me or Ono,</i>

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.340
<i>I don't think we'd get bored</i>
<i>at the arcade.</i>

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.280
HARUO: "WHAT'S UP, KATAGIRI?"

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.950
<i>I thought it'd be nice </i>
<i>to walk home together.</i>

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.620
"SURE, LET'S GO."
"NO THANKS, IT'S EMBARRASSING."

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:13.020
I'll go with
"No thanks, it's embarrassing."

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.460
He's so loyal to Shiori.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.630
Haruo is devoted, isn't he?

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:19.700
Why don't you walk home with her?

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.400
I don't think it's a good idea
to be so cold.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:24.100
Y-You think so?

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.770
<i>Her words carry weight.</i>

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.140
<i>What's this girl's relationship </i>
<i>with Haruo?</i>

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.270
Why don't you give other girls
a call sometime?

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:33.110
Huh? Oh!

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:37.450
Crap! I slept in on the day
of my date with Shiori Fujisaki!

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.980
It's your fault for suddenly
talking to me, Hidaka!

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:41.080
It's my fault?

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.090
And besides, what's with all these bombs?

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:51.130
A COWARD'S LULLABY

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.760
You didn't get a confession
of love from anyone.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.470
What kind of ending is that?

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.770
Toward the end,
most of the girls were upset.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:01.500
What a nice song!

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.510
So how was it? You learned anything
about what women want?

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:06.370
I have no idea.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:09.240
Besides, is what women want
something you can study?

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:12.110
If you play a few more times
you might start to understand.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.350
Yaguchi, I'll let you borrow
the PlayStation for a while longer.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:24.830
But just remember that
I have a bomb, too.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.230
Hey, you!

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:31.130
If you make my sis cry,
mine is gonna go off big time.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:35.300
If you neglect your studies,
your mom's is pretty fearsome, too.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:39.140
I'll call Yoshio-- no, I mean Miyao.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:40.810
See ya.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:49.920
Akira is stressed out as she devotes
herself to Ms. Moemi's lessons.

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:53.960
It's partly my fault as I rebelled
against our family rules.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:58.560
So, I want to help her in any way I can.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.600
You're a caring elder sister.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.770
Hey, do you have plans?

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.330
Something fun that Akira would enjoy?

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:11.340
If Ono can get out for a day,

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:15.240
I want to go with her to the
AOU Show in Makuhari.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.650
An entire day outside, huh?

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.850
Fat chance with the way
Ms. Moemi's been acting.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.020
Isn't there anything?

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:25.590
Something fun, special, and one of a kind?

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:26.990
No, nothing.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.690
Isn't there a game just for Akira
or something?

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.160
Of course no--

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:33.960
RPG MAKER: SUPER DANTE

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.670
There isn't anything like that,
but you can make one!

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:42.400
Something fun, special, and one of a kind.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:44.270
A game just for Ono!

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.780
This is exactly what you asked for.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:49.880
An RPG, so she can let off some steam.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.950
What do you think of
"The Ono Family Quest"?

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:54.020
Sounds nice, sounds nice!

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:57.090
The final boss will be Moemi of course!

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:59.190
If she gets caught, she'll be in trouble.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:04.360
Can you plan something that's fun?

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.830
I'll make something
any gamer would approve of.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:10.130
Games are amazing.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:14.570
You don't just play them, it helps
create relationships with people, too.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.440
I'm leaving things in your hands,
lover boy!

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:20.540
Don't forget to play
<i>Tokimeki Memorial,</i> too!

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.550
What are you doing so seriously?

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:31.690
N-Nothing!

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:34.290
Judging by the way you're flustering,

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:35.860
I'd say you were writing a poem.

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:37.830
Is it a poem, Haruo?

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.560
Right, it's a poem, a poem.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:42.200
You've been pretty cold lately, Haruo.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:46.030
<i>If they find out I'm making </i>
<i>an RPG for Ono...</i>

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:49.570
"My lady, my lady.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:53.380
How about some meat to
recover from your battle?"

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:55.040
What kind of poem is this?

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:00.920
<i>If I were making it</i>
<i>in elementary school,</i>

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:04.590
<i>I'd definitely make the game's objective</i>
<i>to defeat Ono.</i>

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:05.820
ONO QUEST

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:13.300
<i>This is so fun.</i>

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:17.300
<i>Just thinking about Ono playing this game</i>

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.270
<i>makes it fun for me.</i>

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:31.210
Switch... on... off...

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:38.890
No, she'd label this as a lame game.

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:41.990
I always take these kinds
of games for granted,

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:45.360
but making them is really tough.

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:56.470
Akira.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:07:59.810
Moemi's not here, is she?

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:02.610
Come, take a break
and relax in Ziiya's room.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:07.320
Don't worry and just come.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.220
Ladies...

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:11.290
my room is much too dirty...

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:15.520
Is it? Mine is much worse.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:19.290
We just need to use your TV.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:29.770
Haruo made this game
so you can let off some steam.

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:32.710
It took him about 30 days.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:35.240
I helped supervise a bit.

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:37.010
ONO IS AT HOME DOING
HELLISH HOMEWORK AGAIN

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:39.910
Miss Akira is the main character?

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:44.620
Right. Akira faces countless
challenges in this mansion.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.220
GOOD MORNING MISS!

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:48.620
What do you think?

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.290
Do you know how hard it was to make this?

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:54.230
Haruo is a really good guy.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:57.200
<i>Aw, she's blushing.</i>

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:58.530
MONSTERS HAVE APPEARED!

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:00.700
I see.

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:05.970
He's turned her everyday tasks
into the monsters.

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:08.680
That's right.
And by fighting these things,

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:11.710
she'll increase her experience
and level up.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:15.180
This is truly a reflection
of her current situation.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:19.120
For me, this game feels like
young master Haruo's way

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:22.160
to cheer Akira on.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.790
I like that interpretation, Ziiya.

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.800
-It's the shape of love.
-Shh!

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:30.300
ONO FOUND A CANDY!

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.570
YOU PICKED UP A SWEET!

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:35.300
YOU MUST GO, MISS!
GO STICK IT TO THE DEMON LORD MOEMI!

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:37.610
THE GAME ROOM IS LOCKED

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:42.110
<i>That guy really made it well.</i>

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:46.350
Oh, it's the mansion's first boss--

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:49.150
Hey, hey, hey!

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:51.120
What the hell does that mean?!

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:53.220
Why am I the boss?

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:54.590
And in that form, too!

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:57.430
How can he treat me like this
after I helped supervise?!

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:00.700
I take back what I said earlier
about him being a good guy!

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.000
THE NEXT DAY

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:17.310
Miss, taking another break for today?

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:22.280
Please enjoy yourself, Miss.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.290
I'm so happy for her.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:28.760
She finally has a place to
take a breath in the house.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:30.590
THE GAME ROOM

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:33.560
NEW FIGHTING GAME
DRAGOON MIGHT

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:36.760
MEGA MAN SERIES
MEGA MAN: THE POWER BATTLE

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:41.440
DONPACHI
A SHOOTING GAME WITH CRAZY BULLETS!

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:43.570
CYBERBOTS
LET'S FIGHT THE MECHAS!

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:45.540
VIRTUA FIGHTER REMIX
SHOW ME WHAT YOU GOT!

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:48.010
<i>I'll be waiting for you, Ono!</i>

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:12.100
<i>She's been focused on my lessons lately,</i>

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:15.570
<i>I thought my curriculum was</i>
<i>truly effective.</i>

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:21.980
<i>But I see I've made false assumptions!</i>

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:29.450
You will not find what you're looking for.

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:35.960
I told you I will not allow
something like that in the house!

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:39.690
I've gotten rid of it.
No discussion necessary.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.700
THE ONO FAMILY QUEST

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:09.120
Akira?

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:11.260
What a disaster!

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:33.680
Miss Akira. That will be all for today.

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:49.230
Things are so awkward between you.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.700
This must be tough on even you, Ms. Moemi.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:57.510
I was worried what would happen.

00:12:57.570 --> 00:13:00.280
I got scared thinking
she'll run away again.

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:04.850
I only did what was natural
as the educator for the Ono Family.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:09.420
But isn't it tough to teach when
your student puts up a barrier?

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:12.850
It doesn't matter
if it's tough for me or not.

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:15.920
It is my duty to educate Miss Akira.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:18.160
Isn't it painful as a person?

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:20.900
Who's to say.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:23.630
Why do you have to be so stubborn?

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:26.300
Can't you put yourself in Akira's shoes?

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:29.100
She can't go outside,
she can't make friends,

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:32.770
but she endures it and listens to you.

00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:35.840
You threw out her one diversion
without remorse.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:40.180
And now, she has to have lessons
every day with the perpetrator.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.580
Who could stand that?

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:47.390
Do you really think Akira will
grow up to be a decent person?

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:50.630
I also feel the same!

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:55.030
U-Um, please. I don't want you to turn
into an unpleasant person

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.600
for Miss Akira's sake!

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.800
What's with that apron?

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:01.570
Does it not look good on me?

00:14:10.210 --> 00:14:11.310
Phew.

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:15.250
Ms. Moemi.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:17.850
May I have a moment?

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:19.290
Oh, sure.

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:22.420
Would you mind waiting
until I load these?

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:30.900
Ow. Do you work here every day?

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:34.170
Some part-timers just quit,
so they're shorthanded.

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:36.100
I see.

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:39.710
What did you want to talk to me about?

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:42.940
I came here to apologize to you.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.010
Huh? Apologize?

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:52.320
And so, the NES I got rid of
belonged to you.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.090
Allow me to reimburse you.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.060
The Twin Famicom!

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:58.090
Why did you get this?

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:03.200
I asked them to give me one version above
the NES console at the game shop.

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:07.700
<i>Here's another adult who calls </i>
<i>every and any console an "NES".</i>

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:12.910
Did something happen with Ono?

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:16.380
She hates me now.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:21.950
I understand her less and less these days.

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:26.120
How do you feel about Miss Akira?

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:27.760
How do I feel?

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:30.360
She's like a wall I can't overcome.

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:33.190
But she's a woman I respect.

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:35.900
She's someone I want to play games with.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:38.600
She's weird, but that's
what's interesting about her.

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:40.600
When she's in trouble, I want to help her.

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:45.810
I want to be someone
who can be there for her.

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:49.410
Mr. Haruo, do you realize
what those feelings mean?

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:50.510
Huh?

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:53.710
Haruo, the manager's asking for you!

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:56.320
Okay! Excuse me.

00:15:57.690 --> 00:15:58.890
Ms. Moemi.

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:03.360
I think Ono would like you better
without those weird glasses.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:19.310
I'm so glad you invited me
to the "Aou Show" today!

00:16:19.570 --> 00:16:21.540
I told you, it's the A-O-U Show.

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.210
Hurry, hurry!

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:29.180
<i>Haruo.</i>

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:32.450
<i>Wait, Haruo!</i>

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:41.760
<i>Just wait there a moment, Haruo.</i>

00:16:42.930 --> 00:16:45.230
Why'd you stop?

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.840
The light turned red now.

00:16:57.750 --> 00:16:59.010
Akira?

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:01.050
Is that umbrella...

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:05.720
<i>Will you go return this umbrella for me?</i>

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:09.390
<i>They lent it to me when I went to </i>
<i>the Yaguchis' a while ago.</i>

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:13.430
<i>And, let's call it a day for today.</i>

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:18.930
Coincidences like this just don't happen.

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:24.570
This is the game gods telling you
to go to the "Aou Show" with Akira.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:27.110
B-But what about you, Mom?

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:29.210
Be a man, Haruo!

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:32.980
Use everything you learned
from <i>Tokimeki Memorial</i> today!

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:39.550
Go, Haruo!

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:55.070
Are all these people
going to the AOU Show?

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:34.540
Incredible! This is where the forefront of
the forefront of the arcade era gathers!

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:38.010
I don't even know where we should start.

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:40.980
Is there a game maker
you wanna start with?

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.220
I get you, Ono.

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:47.120
Your gamer spirit is all abuzz, right?

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:49.990
Or do you need to pee?

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:51.230
Ow!

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:00.430
It's gonna be Voldo for me.

00:19:01.170 --> 00:19:04.210
<i>Ono went with Rock, </i>
<i>her usual heavyweight type.</i>

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:09.780
<i>Ono's a quick learner as usual.</i>

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:13.210
<i>Oh, now I'm getting all fired up.</i>

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:20.190
<i>It's my goal to someday </i>
<i>bring her to her knees!</i>

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:25.690
<i>I was planning on using that fighter!</i>

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:29.430
<i>This is the first time we wanted</i>
<i>to use the same characters.</i>

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:32.630
TAKE HOME AN INCREDIBLE GAME.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:36.440
The AOU Show is way more impressive
than I imagined.

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:40.680
There are games
no matter which way you turn!

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:43.340
Home games are gradually evolving,

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:46.050
but arcade games are still contenders!

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.090
<i>It reminds me of back then.</i>

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:59.430
<i>But she seems more cheerful than before.</i>

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:05.200
You're wondering
why I'm staring like a dummy?

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:07.640
I was just thinking you're so excited.

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:11.310
What? Oh, I'm being annoying
so you're stepping on my foot?

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:13.370
Ouch.

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:20.150
Man, didn't think we'd win so much.

00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:22.480
The latest crane games were
all-you-can-play,

00:20:22.550 --> 00:20:24.320
and the gifts were all-you-can-carry!

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:26.320
I almost fell over in surprise.

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.320
It was pretty fun, right?

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:33.060
Oh, I'm glad you seem satisfied.

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:38.030
The station is probably crowded now.
Wanna go eat something?

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:40.740
-Did you see episode eight?
-Of course!

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:42.270
Asuka's the best!

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:46.510
Is that the only way you can eat?

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:51.950
The gaming industry can be intense!

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:55.050
<i>Virtua Fighter 2 </i>is portable on the
Sega Saturn and<i> Street Fighter Alpha, </i>too!

00:20:55.420 --> 00:21:00.520
In the meantime, <i>Fighting Vipers</i>
and <i>Soul Edge</i> will be in the arcades!

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:03.290
I need to focus on Polygon games, too.

00:21:03.590 --> 00:21:08.030
But if I neglect my schoolwork,
I'll be in trouble...

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:16.740
<i>She's really listening to me.</i>

00:21:17.070 --> 00:21:20.510
<i>What if this was a girl</i>
<i>who wasn't interested in games?</i>

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:28.220
<i>I can't come up with anything</i>
<i>if I try to have a normal conversation.</i>

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:35.690
<i>She's quiet, but I guess </i>
<i>she doesn't like the silence either.</i>

00:21:45.600 --> 00:21:48.570
Seems like there's
a bunch of unnecessary stuff.

00:21:49.300 --> 00:21:51.410
Oh right, I forgot.

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:54.380
You enjoy anything you get.

00:21:56.610 --> 00:21:57.850
That reminds me,

00:21:57.910 --> 00:22:00.350
your sis and I struggled with
the crane game

00:22:00.410 --> 00:22:02.820
trying to get you something
to cheer you up before.

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:05.920
Which prize did you like the best?

00:22:06.490 --> 00:22:11.190
For me it was the mini fan that
had a lot of practical use.

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:45.830
Everything seems so impressive
when I'm with you.

00:22:47.960 --> 00:22:50.830
Let's go together again next time.

00:23:11.350 --> 00:23:13.350
Your house is huge.

00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:15.220
You can see it even from here.

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:18.830
You can get home
on your own from here, right?

00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:25.770
Not yet?

00:23:29.770 --> 00:23:31.640
You don't want to go home yet?

00:23:42.450 --> 00:23:44.850
T-Tonight--

00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:46.890
Miss!

00:23:46.950 --> 00:23:51.560
I was just about to go pick you up
since it was getting late!

00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:55.030
Hmm? I've hit something familiar...

00:23:59.070 --> 00:24:02.140
<i>This reminds me of back then, too.</i>

00:24:03.640 --> 00:24:05.970
Subtitle translation by
Emily Noguchi
